// Conflicting objects definitions for TR2: The Golden Mask. In a situation
// when two different objects share the same IDs, the objects register
// themselves as usual through the C constructor mechanism, and fight for the
// slot. The conflict is currently resolved by an external party – in terms of
// the Golden Mask, this currently happens in Shell_Main(), that manually calls
// the setup routine overriding whatever information was in the slot.
//
// TODO: this aliasing mechanism needs to go away in favor of injections-only
// approach that patches the problematic items to use specific objects of
// specific UUID.
OBJ_ID_ALIAS_DEFINE(O_MONK_3, O_MONK_1)
OBJ_ID_ALIAS_DEFINE(O_BEAR,   O_BIG_SPIDER)
OBJ_ID_ALIAS_DEFINE(O_WOLF,   O_SPIDER)
